      de: ["The Guadalquivir Basin covers a total area of approximately 35,000 square kilometers.", "It is the only major Spanish river valley that widely opens towards the Atlantic without significant coastal mountains.", "The region was an arm of the sea during the Miocene, gradually filling with marine and fluvial sediments.", "It is the center of Spain's olive oil production, often called the 'Olive Grove of Europe'.", "The Doñana National Park at the river's mouth was declared a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1994.", "The Guadalquivir is the only navigable river in Spain, allowing ships to reach the inland port of Seville.", "The basin experiences a Mediterranean climate with oceanic influences, featuring very hot summers and mild winters."],
